 "caption_en": "If countries were animals. Not by vibes. By data. 🐾\n\n🇳🇱 Netherlands = beaver: 26% of the country is below sea level, so it builds dams and dikes (PBL Netherlands Environmental Assessment Agency, 2010).\n🇨🇭 Switzerland = ibex: the last Swiss ibex was shot in 1809; in 1906 Switzerland smuggled ibex kids back from Italy. About 17,000 live there today (Swissinfo, 2017).\n🇯🇵 Japan = tortoise: 107,677 people aged 100 or more (Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare, Sept 2026).\n🇦🇪 UAE = falcon: falcons get passports; more than 28,000 issued since 2002 (Environment Agency Abu Dhabi via Gulf News, 2018).\n🇮🇱 Israel = hedgehog: small (about 22,000 km², roughly 0.015% of the world's land, our math: Israel CBS 22,072 km² ÷ Earth's land 148.9 million km²), spiky (Iron Dome intercepted about 90% of the rockets it engaged over populated areas in 2014, IDF) and still cuddly: 8th happiest country on Earth (World Happiness Report 2026).\n\nSmall, spiky, happy.\n\nWhich animal is your country? Tell me in the comments.\n\nPhotos (Wikimedia Commons): Giles Laurent (CC BY-SA 4.0); Bouke ten Cate (CC BY 4.0); Denkrahm (CC BY 4.0); Lisa James (CC BY 4.0); Denise Chan (CC BY-SA 2.0); Yuriy75 (CC BY-SA 3.0); Israel Defense Forces (CC BY 2.0); Dan Harrelson (CC BY 2.0). AI voice.",
 "caption_he": "אם מדינות היו חיות. לא לפי תחושה, לפי נתונים.\nהולנד בונה (26% מתחת לפני הים), שווייץ יעל (הוברחו בחזרה מאיטליה ב־1906), יפן צב (107,677 בני 100 ומעלה), איחוד האמירויות בז (לבזים יש דרכונים).\nוישראל? קיפוד. קטנה, דוקרנית, ושמינית בעולם באושר.\nאיזו חיה המדינה שלכם?",
